    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0647" n="1325" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1325"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 428.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 10, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of October 21 (No. 366) has
                    been received.</p>
                <p>The subject of a license for the exportation of the French tobacco through our
                    blockade has been heretofore much discussed here with a disposition to do an act
                    of liberality towards the imperial government. But recently that disposition has
                    been much embarrassed by the proceedings at Brest in regard to the Florida, and
                    the discovery of the armament of pirates at Nantes and Bordeaux, for hostilities
                        <pb facs="0648" n="1326" xml:id="pg1326"/> against the United States. The
                    subject will again be considered by the President, in view of the very prompt
                    and honorable proceedings of the imperial government in arresting the armaments
                    in the French ports, and Mr. Mercier will be informed of the decision.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
